================================================================================
1. OVERVIEW
================================================================================

reverseshell.py is a professional-grade reverse shell client written in
Python 3. A reverse shell works the opposite way of a traditional shell: the
target machine (the "implant") initiates an outbound connection to the
attacker's machine (the "listener"), which makes it useful in authorized
security assessments where inbound connections are blocked by firewalls.

Once connected, the operator can:

- Execute any system command (whoami, ipconfig, dir, ...)
- Execute PowerShell commands with execution policy bypass
- Download / upload files to and from the target
- Take screenshots of the target's screen
- Install persistence mechanisms (registry or scheduled task)
- Gather system information in JSON format
- Manage processes (list and kill)
- Download and execute payloads remotely
- Automatically reconnect if the connection drops


================================================================================
2. REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

2.1 On the target machine (implant)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Operating system : Windows (primary) / Linux (partial support)
Python           : 3.6 or newer
Permissions      : No admin rights required for most commands

2.2 On the attacker machine (listener)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Nmap / Ncat      : REQUIRED - used to receive the connection
Any OS           : Windows, Linux, macOS

WHY NCAT?
Ncat is the modern reimplementation of Netcat, included in the Nmap suite.
It provides the listening socket that accepts the incoming connection from
the implant and lets you type commands interactively.


================================================================================
3. INSTALLING NMAP (WITH NCAT)
================================================================================

3.1 Windows
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Download the installer from the official site: https://nmap.org/download.html
2. Choose the nmap-<version>-setup.exe installer (or the zip version).
3. Run the installer. Keep the default installation path
   (usually C:\Program Files (x86)\Nmap\).
4. Verify the installation by opening a new terminal and running:

   & "C:\Program Files (x86)\Nmap\ncat.exe" --version

   You should see output similar to:

   Ncat: Version 7.80 ( https://nmap.org/ncat )

5. (Optional) Add the Nmap folder to your PATH so you can type "ncat"
   instead of the full path:

   [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable("Path", $env:Path + ";C:\Program Files (x86)\Nmap", "User")

3.2 Linux (Debian/Ubuntu/Kali)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   sudo apt update
   sudo apt install nmap
   ncat --version

3.3 macOS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   brew install nmap
   ncat --version


================================================================================
4. INSTALLATION OF THE REVERSE SHELL
================================================================================

1. Copy reverseshell.py to the target machine.

2. (Recommended) Create a Python virtual environment:

   cd C:\path\to\your\folder
   python -m venv .venv
   .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

3. No third-party packages are required - the script only uses Python's
   standard library (socket, subprocess, os, base64, ...).

4. (Optional) Edit the configuration block at the top of the file:

   HOST = "127.0.0.1"       # IP of the listener (attacker machine)
