================================================================================
7. HOW IT WORKS (TECHNICAL DETAILS)
================================================================================

7.1 Connection flow
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Implant]                         [Listener (ncat)]
    |                                     |
    |---- TCP connect (outbound) -------->|
    |<--- banner: Connected | hostname ---|
    |<--- command prompt "> " ------------|
    |                                     |
    |<--------- command ----------------  |
    |--------- command output ----------->|
    |<--------- command ----------------  |
    |--------- command output ----------->|
    ...

1. The implant resolves HOST:PORT and creates a TCP socket.
2. It connects outbound, which is why firewalls rarely block it.
3. The listener receives the connection and displays the banner.
4. Both sides exchange lines of text: commands in, output out.
5. If the connection dies, the implant waits RECONNECT_DELAY seconds and
   tries again - indefinitely by default.

7.2 Command execution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Commands are decoded from UTF-8 and stripped of whitespace.
- Built-in commands (cd, ls, download, ...) are handled directly in Python.
- Everything else goes through subprocess.run() with cmd.exe /c (Windows)
  or sh -c (Linux), capturing both stdout and stderr.
- Output is truncated at MAX_OUTPUT (2 MB) to avoid flooding the socket.

7.3 File transfer (download / upload / screenshot)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Files are read into memory and encoded as Base64.
- The data is sent in 4 KB chunks with a small delay between chunks to
  avoid overflowing the socket buffer.
- A [FILE] header announces name, size, and SHA-256 hash.
- The transfer ends with an EOF marker.
- The SHA-256 digest lets the operator verify integrity after the transfer.

7.4 Screenshot
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Uses a PowerShell one-liner with System.Windows.Forms and System.Drawing
  to capture the primary screen to a PNG in %TEMP%.
- The PNG is then exfiltrated through the same file-transfer mechanism.

7.5 Persistence
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two methods are available (Windows only):

   Method    Technique
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------
   runkey    Adds an entry to HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run
   task      Registers a scheduled task triggered AtLogOn (default)

The scheduled task approach uses pythonw.exe when available so the implant
runs without a visible console window.

7.6 Reconnection and shutdown
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- RECONNECT_DELAY (default 5 s) controls how long the implant waits between
  attempts.
- MAX_RECONNECTS = -1 means infinite retries; set a positive number to limit
  them.
- Typing "die" creates a .stop marker file next to the script. On the next
  loop iteration the implant checks for this file and exits permanently.


