9. LIMITATIONS (HONEST DISCLOSURE)
================================================================================

- Plaintext traffic: this ncat version sends commands and output in
  cleartext - anyone sniffing the network can read them. For encrypted
  operation, use the AES-GCM version of the tool instead.

- No authentication: ncat does not verify who connects. Anyone who can reach
  the port could connect to your listener.

- Memory usage: file transfers load the whole file into RAM.

- Windows-oriented: screenshots and persistence are Windows-only.

- AV detection: as a known reverse-shell pattern, it is flagged by most
  antivirus engines. This is expected and by design.

- Python dependency: the target needs a Python interpreter unless you
  compile it to a standalone EXE with PyInstaller:

     pip install pyinstaller
     pyinstaller --onefile --noconsole --name update reverseshell.py


